-- title:
--   Concrete Tests and Sequential Relaxation Equivalence
-- statement:
--   This is the abstract relaxation bridge for a pre-energy.
--
--   Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on a measurable space, let $P$ be a pre-energy on the real $L^2(\mu)$ space, and let $C\in\mathbb{NNReal}$. Then the finite constant $C$ works on the concrete test family generated by $P$ if and only if it works on the finite domain of the sequential relaxation of $P$:
--
--   $$\mathrm{Holds}_{\mathrm{ofPreEnergy}(\mu,P)}(C)
--   \iff \mathrm{Holds}_{\mathrm{L2Energy}(\mu,\,P.\mathrm{sequentialRelaxation})}(C).$$
--
--   The statement is an abstract comparison result and allows empty test types and infinite optimal constants.
-- source:
--   Lean source: https://github.com/human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean/blob/408915f/formalization/FunctionalInequalities/Poincare/Relaxation.lean#L36-L57 (repository human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean, commit 408915f, module `FunctionalInequalities.Poincare.Relaxation`, declaration `FunctionalInequalities.Poincare.TestFamily.holds_ofPreEnergy_iff`; the repository is private at upload time).

